@startuml graph-pivot
title US-14: Graph Pivot - Operator Explores Entity Relationship Network

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

actor Operator
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
participant "Express API" as API
database "Neo4j\nentity graph" as Neo4j

Operator -> Dashboard : clicks "Show related entities"\non VesselB in investigation view

Dashboard -> API : GET /entities/VesselB/relationships?since=24h

API -> Neo4j : MATCH (b:Entity {id: 'VesselB'})-[e:PROXIMITY_EVENT]-(other:Entity)\nWHERE e.timestamp_ms > $since_ms\nRETURN other.id,\n  collect(e) AS events,\n  exists((b)-[:KNOWN_ASSOCIATE]-(other)) AS known\nORDER BY size(events) DESC

note over Neo4j
  Variable-depth traversal from a single node.
  Returns all entities that came within
  proximity of VesselB in the last 24 hours,
  with edge properties and relationship flags.
  In SQL this is a self-join on a proximity
  events table - expensive as density grows.
  In Neo4j it is a single pattern match.
end note

Neo4j --> API : [ { entity_id, event_count,\n  closest_approach_metres,\n  known: bool }, ... ]

API --> Dashboard : relationship network\n{ nodes: [...], edges: [...] }

Dashboard --> Operator : network graph rendered\n- VesselB at centre\n- known associates in grey\n- unknown entities highlighted\n- edge weight = number of proximity events

note over Operator
  Operator spots VesselC made 3 approaches
  to VesselB after it went dark - all flagged
  as unknown. Clicks VesselC to pivot and
  open its own investigation view.
end note

Operator -> Dashboard : clicks VesselC node
Dashboard -> API : GET /entities/VesselC/relationships?since=24h

note over API
  Same query, different starting node.
  The pivot pattern works for any entity
  without additional API design.
end note

@enduml
